        },
        {
         "t": "heading",
         "level": "h2",
         "text": "What Should a Small Business Website Include?",
         "align": "left",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "text",
         "html": "<p>A small business website should answer three questions within a few seconds: what you do, where you do it and how to reach you. That means a clear headline, your services in plain language, real photos or examples of your work, and a phone number or quote button that is always easy to tap.</p><p>Everything else supports those basics. Pages should load quickly on a phone, read well for visitors and search engines, and look like the same business that is on your truck, cards and storefront. We design with that consistency in mind because a website that does not match your logo can make customers wonder if they found the right company.</p>",
         "align": "left",
         "classes": []
        },
        {
         "t": "list",
         "items": [
          {
           "text": "A homepage that explains your business in one glance",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          },
          {
           "text": "Service, about and contact sections written for customers",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          },
          {
           "text": "Tap-to-call and quote buttons on every screen size",
           "icon": "fas fa-check-circle"
          }
         ],
         "classes": []
        }
       ]
      },
