    {
     "t": "heading",
     "level": "h2",
     "text": "How Much Does a Small Business Website Cost in Austin?",
     "align": "left",
     "classes": []
    },
    {
     "t": "text",
     "html": "<p>At Logo Design Austin, the Business Starter Package is $950. It includes a custom logo (JPG and PNG), a basic single-page responsive website with multiple sections, 150 business cards, Google Business Profile setup, a free domain and hosting for the first year, Google Search Console submission and free website maintenance for the first year. From the second year, maintenance is $250 per year and an optional yearly backup is $50. See the <a href=\"/business-packages/\">Business Starter Package</a> page for full details.</p><h3>Websites for new businesses in East Austin (78702), Mueller (78723) and Hyde Park (78751)</h3><p>New shops, studios and food businesses often need a logo, a simple site and business cards all at once. The starter package covers those first pieces so you can open with a consistent look.</p><h3>Contractor and home service websites in Round Rock (78664), Pflugerville (78660) and Kyle (78640)</h3><p>Service businesses benefit most from a site that lists services clearly, shows real work and puts the phone number front and center for visitors searching on their phones.</p><h3>Professional and practice websites near Downtown (78701) and the Domain (78758)</h3><p>Law offices, clinics and consultants need a calm, credible site that explains who they help and makes scheduling a consultation easy.</p><h3>Can a website guarantee I rank first on Google?</h3><p>No one can honestly guarantee a specific ranking. Rankings depend on competition and ongoing SEO work. What a well-built site does is give Google and your customers clear, accurate information to work with.</p>",
     "align": "left",
     "classes": []
    },
